  <title>Braille output</title>
  <p>
    Read content with a refreshable braille display and control its reading location.
  </p>
  <p>
    Braille displays communicate with Orca through BRLTTY, a service that connects braille
    displays to applications. Configure your display in BRLTTY before enabling braille output.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can pan the braille display, return to the current location, route the cursor, or mark
    text for copying. Standard keyboard bindings can be changed in Commands preferences. Braille
    display bindings depend on the display and BRLTTY configuration and cannot be rebound in
    Orca.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cursor routing moves the caret to the character at a selected braille cell or activates the
    item at that cell. To copy text, use Cut Begin at its start and Cut Line at its end. Orca
    selects the text and copies it to the clipboard; paste it using the destination
    application's usual paste command.
  </p>
